From ffdd45a2efc81f16df274e9454b56e1c1c082f3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:27:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/46] goddard: remove the function-local `UNUSED u8
 fillerN[]` stack padding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

These arrays exist to reproduce the ROM's stack-frame layout for the
matching build; they are never read or written and the UNUSED attribute
is the only reason the compiler tolerates them. 144 declarations across
13 file(s) in goddard/. Struct members are untouched — the fillers
that fix a layout (save files, object rawData, audio structs) all live in
headers, which this patch does not visit.

Verified: every file compiles to byte-identical assembly before and after
with the port's own flags (asmdiff over compile_commands.json).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/goddard/debug_utils.c   |  4 ----
 src/goddard/draw_objects.c  | 16 ----------------
